nce":{"authority_availability":"available","authority_receipt_ref":"receipts/acceptance/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime_fixture_acceptance.json","evidence_class":"bounded_runtime_computation","fresh_run_status":"not_run_by_index","historical_receipt_refs":["receipts/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime_result.json","receipts/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime_board.json","receipts/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime_validation_receipt.json","receipts/acceptance/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime_fixture_acceptance.json"],"receipt_time_basis":"historical_saved_artifact"},"formal_subclaim_ids":[],"primary_guide_id":"paper_module.semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime","primary_guide_ref":"paper_modules/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime.md","registered_runner_ref":"src/microcosm_core/organs/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime.py","replay_id":"replay::semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime","requirements_review":{"status":"unrecorded"},"summary":"Exercises command-run deduplication using keys derived from inputs and environment.","title":"Deduplicate matching local command runs"},"claim_ceiling":"keys and dedups command runs by repo-state fingerprint; does not guarantee global mutual exclusion, does not replace a lock service, and does not prove cross-host correctness","claim_ceiling_restated":"Builds a run key from the command arguments, working directory, repository state, scoped file content, resource class and the `PYTHONPATH` and `PYTEST_ADDOPTS` values, shares or reuses results for matching runs on one machine, and rejects an empty command.","claim_id":"claim::semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime","evidence_class":"bounded_runtime_computation","evidence_strength_rank":4,"organ_id":"semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_runtime_receipt","validator_command":"python -m microcosm_core.organs.semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime run --input fixtures/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime/input --out receipts/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime --acceptance-out receipts/acceptance/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime_fixture_acceptance.json"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"5d94ca45ff5e68783e2a7fa9436e649bc6fdf8b1df32c0dd5bd15b738240fa98","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"bounded_runtime_computation","family":"work_landing_and_continuity","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_runtime_receipt"},"component_id":"semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime","plain":"Running the same command again and again wastes time when nothing it depends on has changed. This component is given a command runner and temporary example commands to run through it as local processes. For each request it builds a label from the command, its folder, the project's state, the contents of the files that matter and a few settings, so requests with the same label can share one run. The output is a saved result showing which requester ran the command and which reused its answer, and a change to one of those files gives a new label.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime.md","sha256":"65bcaff63986aea51ac6b510232d14c655ab57e1b3f605ffdae4f1636e7ab744","text":"# Deduplicate matching local command runs\n\n> **In plain terms.** Running the same command again and again wastes time when nothing it depends on has changed. This component is given a command runner and temporary example commands to run through it as local processes. For each request it builds a label from the command, its folder, the project's state, the contents of the files that matter and a few settings, so requests with the same label can share one run. The output is a saved result showing which requester ran the command and which reused its answer, and a change to one of those files gives a new label.\n\nThe fixture exercises a command runner that builds a key from command arguments, working directory, repository state, scoped file content, resource class, and the `PYTHONPATH` and `PYTEST_ADDOPTS` environment values. Matching runs can share or reuse a result; the fixture also checks that a scoped file change changes the key. It writes a result, board and validation receipt.\n\n## Run the example\n\nFrom the repository root, with Python 3.11 or newer and the checkout dependencies available:\n\n```sh\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime run \\\n  --input fixtures/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime/input \\\n  --out .microcosm/component-guides/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime \\\n  --acceptance-out .microcosm/component-guides/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime/acceptance.json\n```\n\nInspect `.microcosm/component-guides/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime_result.json` for the result and findings.\n\nThe runner stores local run state and distinguishes the process that executes the command from callers that reuse its result. The fixture checks those roles with temporary commands; inspect the individual cases in the result.\n\n## What the result means\n\nAn empty command is rejected, and changed scoped content must not reuse the old key. Other environment values are not part of the key, so callers must account for changes that could affect a command. The tests use local processes and temporary state; they do not establish a distributed lock or cross-host correctness.\n\n## Verification\n\nWhen `make component-replays` runs this component, the shared [Dafny-verified replay admission](../formal/replay/README.md) checks observed source and input identities, claim-policy identity, and receipt agreement. The example above runs directly and does not invoke that gate. There is no component-specific formal proof of the deduplication algorithm; local tests do not establish cross-host behavior.\n\n## Source\n\n[Implementation](../src/microcosm_core/organs/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime.py) · [command runner](../src/microcosm_core/engine_room/command_run_singleflight.py) · [input](../fixtures/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime/input) · [tests](../tests/test_semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime.py) · [historical sample result](../receipts/acceptance/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime_fixture_acceptance.json) · [component record](../core/paper_module_capsules.json).\n"},"proofs":[],"replay":{"command":"make component-replays","command_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_replays.py","command_scope":"all registered components","configuration_refs":["src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#RUNTIME_STEPS","src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#_accepted_organ_runner_module_refs"],"declared_prerequisites":{"availability_status":"not_assessed_by_index","description":"Lean, Swift and test extras required","source_ref":"Makefile"},"execution_status":"not_run_by_index","fresh_receipt_template":".microcosm/component-replays/<run>/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime_result.json","guide_example":{"command":"microcosm semantic-singleflight-dedup-runtime run --input fixtures/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime/input --out receipts/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime --acceptance-out receipts/acceptance/first_wave/semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime_fixture_acceptance.json","expected_result_description":{"status":"unrecorded"},"prerequisites_description":{"se